-- ============================================================================
-- 20260721_exercise_metadata_and_taxonomy.sql — Step 4.3 prerequisite
-- ============================================================================
-- Populates the rich per-row metadata columns (equipment, category, difficulty,
-- target_muscle, secondary_muscles) and the exercise_taxonomy lookup table that
-- 20260719_exercise_catalog_enrichment.sql (4.2a) added but never actually filled
-- in — confirmed live: all 2,126 rows had NULL/empty values for these columns
-- and exercise_taxonomy had 0 rows before this migration.
--
-- Coverage: only the 760 `free-exercise-db`-sourced rows get equipment/category/
-- difficulty/target_muscle/secondary_muscles here, matched exactly by source_id
-- against scratch/free-exercise-db/dist/exercises.json (760/760 matched, 0
-- misses). The other 1,366 rows (omercotkd-gifs, exercisegymgifsdb) have no
-- equivalent structured metadata source — a name-based fuzzy match against
-- free-exercise-db only covers ~8-9% of them, too low-confidence to be worth
-- the risk of mismatched equipment/category data, so they're left NULL rather
-- than guessed. muscle_group and body_part already have 100% coverage from
-- 4.2a's URL-derived backfill, so muscle-group and body-part filtering still
-- works across the whole catalog — only the equipment/category/difficulty
-- filters are scoped to the ~36% of the catalog that has that data.
-- ============================================================================

-- Auto-generated backfill values for free-exercise-db rows, source_id -> (equipment, category, difficulty, target_muscle, secondary_muscles)
-- Generated from scratch/free-exercise-db/dist/exercises.json against live source_id values (760 rows)
